Mechanisms
- src/ring/journal.rs in bbt-supervisor: BBR1 frame+CRC32C, nil-seat tick commits, one barrier per tick, bounded staging, strong flushes, 64MiB rotation, coverage-based retirement and CRC-valid whole-tick recovery.
- Checkpoints prefix the unchanged Saved payload with JCP2 + journal ULID + offset (28bytes), covering parsed input rather than the publication tail. Legacy8byte records remain readable.
- Writer keeps bounded tail refs and row indexes; derived ring+tail history is paged. Old-process journal retention is conservative when its sealed-projection proof is unavailable.
- Admission locks enforce undurable byte/time debt and one admission tick per seat. Query replies and commit boundaries wake the actor; raw append credit release does not force an O(seats) poller pass.
- Child-status polling has100ms cadence, immediate EOF/due-escalation checks. Event-driven reaping is separately queued as W1.2e; no additional runtime or worker pool.
- Logic retries rejected capture Busy only, keeps checkpoint cursors on rejection, preserves pending events and serves later commands. No ambiguous effects/input retries.

